[x] Inventory the homed Darrion home before the drive is reused =homed-inventory $Unlocked 2026-10-21. Darrion runs sudo sh ~/darrion-inventory.sh > ~/darrion-inventory.txt on the desktop (read-only: sizes, git repos with unpushed work, files changed since May); the facilitator sorts it into already elsewhere and only here.$ +human ^2026-10-21T00:04 %2026-10-21T00:20 #01a15bc6-5a1c-7461-bd35-b7937bb4cfb5
[_] Boot the desktop image from the USB NVMe =portable-desktop $The machine that travels. Needs the image's Secure Boot keys enrolled on each host (or Secure Boot off for USB boot), and a passphrase or FIDO2 unlock, since a TPM belongs to one machine.$ ^2026-10-21T00:04 %2026-10-21T00:20 <desktop-profile <retire-homed #01a15bc6-5a51-7c92-96a1-646f371a0599
[x] Decide where the desktop package list lives =desktop-list-home $NEEDS DECISION: A, chezmoi packages.yaml installs on today's Arch desktop and moves to personal-os later; B, a personal-os desktop profile (not yet booted) is the list now and today's desktop installs from it, so the image is the inventory. On personal-os /usr is read-only, so a chezmoi pacman installer has no future there.$ +human ^2026-10-21T00:04 %2026-10-21T01:35 #01a15bc6-5a38-7f61-a121-7d3281a2af35
[x] Sort the desktop's software into layers or drop =desktop-sort $The 164 unlisted packages plus user level (Flatpaks, user units, ~/.local, the AUR set), each into one row of the layer table or drop. The facilitator drafts it grouped by purpose; Darrion makes the calls. Docker, docker-compose and podman are proposed drops. Draft 2026-10-21 in docs/desktop-sort/ (README has the six shaping calls and the pruning list).$ ^2026-10-21T00:04 %2026-10-21T01:55 #01a15bc6-5a30-7963-875a-79fd55448791
